            Size the purchase around the pail. A 5-gallon pail does a typical two-car driveway in one heavy coat or a patio in two, and on anything past two or three gallons the pail is usually the simpler buy, so compare per-gallon prices. Buy the gallon for steps, walks and small slabs. Do not overbuy for future years: Foundation Armor gives a shelf life of up to a year in a properly sealed container, and at a 10-year recoat interval leftover sealer will be long past its date. Our <a href="/how-much-concrete-sealer-do-i-need/">concrete sealer calculator guide</a> covers the measuring in more detail.
