        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the right SX5000 is the water-based WB: a 5-gallon pail for a driveway or patio, a 1-gallon bottle for steps and walks, and the 16 oz sample first if the surface is pavers, stone or colored concrete. Foundation Armor gives it the same coverage, traffic times and up-to-10-year claim as the solvent version, without the flammability and respirator requirement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the solvent SX5000 only for bare exterior concrete where you want the 40% solids and can apply it safely. And buy neither if you want a wet look or oil-stain protection, because a silane-siloxane does not do either.
